-- scja3-sch6-sixth-schedule.l4: the Sixth Schedule (civil appeals to be made to the Court of Appeal).
-- Layer 1, written from the text alone (SCJA1969.txt lines 6172-6263).  Answers seam 8 of PLAN.md; the asking section is s 29C(2), in scja1's range.
-- JUST TRUE: the Schedule says the appeal is made to the Court of Appeal.  JUST FALSE: no limb of the Schedule holds (s 29C(2) hands the question to
-- "the Sixth Schedule or any other written law", and limb (j) takes in every other written law).  NOTHING: outside the Schedule's scope.

§ `Sixth Schedule: civil appeals to be made to the Court of Appeal`

-- Limb (i): the written law an appeal is made under, from the eight the Schedule names.
DECLARE `sch 6 para 1(i) the provision the appeal is made under` IS ONE OF
    `sch 6 para 1(i)(i) section 32(1) of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016`
    `sch 6 para 1(i)(ii) section 21A(1), 45(7) or 49(11) of the Arbitration Act 2001`
    `sch 6 para 1(i)(iii) section 74(4) of the Competition Act 2004`
    `sch 6 para 1(i)(iv) section 10(4) of the International Arbitration Act 1994`
    `sch 6 para 1(i)(v) section 18(5) of the Maintenance of Parents Act 1995`
    `sch 6 para 1(i)(vi) section 90(3) of the Patents Act 1994`
    `sch 6 para 1(i)(vii) section 35(4) of the Personal Data Protection Act 2012 as in force immediately before 1 February 2021, or section 48R(4) of that Act`
    `sch 6 para 1(i)(viii) section 17(8), 29(9), 35(7) or 44(9) of the Protection from Online Falsehoods and Manipulation Act 2019`
    `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions`

-- Helper: one answer from several limbs.  Any limb that holds gives JUST TRUE; limbs that all fail give JUST FALSE; an unanswered limb leaves NOTHING.
GIVEN limbs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 the limbs taken together` MEANS
    IF elem (JUST TRUE) limbs
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF elem NOTHING limbs
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Sixth Schedule or any other written law so provides" (s 29C(2)), "in the following cases" (para 1) [handed to a list, and no head in the list holds; delegated-definition ruling (a) of 2026-11-05]
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The Schedule's scope: "an appeal against a decision of the General Division in the exercise of its original or appellate civil jurisdiction".
-- The Singapore International Commercial Court is spoken of by limb (f), so it is in scope; the Family Division of the High Court is not named (fork S3-K1).
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 1 the court is the General Division or the Singapore International Commercial Court` MEANS
    decision's `made by` EQUALS `General Division` OR decision's `made by` EQUALS `Singapore International Commercial Court`

GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 1 the jurisdiction is original or appellate` MEANS
    decision's `in the exercise of` EQUALS `original jurisdiction` OR decision's `in the exercise of` EQUALS `appellate jurisdiction`

GIVEN decision IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`sch 6 para 1 the decision is within the Schedule's scope` MEANS
    `sch 6 para 1 the court is the General Division or the Singapore International Commercial Court` decision
    AND `sch 6 para 1 the jurisdiction is original or appellate` decision
    AND decision's `nature of the proceeding` EQUALS `a civil proceeding`

