-- Seam 8 of PLAN.md.
GIVEN decision IS A Decision
      provision IS A `sch 6 para 1(i) the provision the appeal is made under`
      `the appeal is made under a written law that provides for the appeal to lie to the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal made under a written law (other than the Acts the Sixth Schedule names) that says the appeal lies to the Court of Appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    IF `sch 6 para 1 the decision is within the Schedule's scope` decision
    THEN `sch 6 the limbs taken together` (LIST
              `sch 6 para 1(a) the appeal arises from a case relating to constitutional or administrative law` decision
            , `sch 6 para 1(b) the appeal arises from a case relating to contempt of court` decision
            , `sch 6 para 1(c) the appeal arises from a case relating to the law of arbitration` decision
            , `sch 6 para 1(d) the appeal arises from a case relating to the insolvency, restructuring or dissolution of a corporation, limited liability partnership or sub-fund` decision
            , `sch 6 para 1(e) the appeal arises from a case relating to the law of patents` decision
            , `sch 6 para 1(ea) the appeal arises from a case relating to admiralty law or shipping law` decision
            , `sch 6 para 1(f) the appeal is against a decision of the Singapore International Commercial Court` decision
            , `sch 6 para 1(g) the appeal is against a decision or order under the Parliamentary Elections Act 1954` decision
            , `sch 6 para 1(h) the appeal is against a judgment or order in an action under section 47(8) of the Presidential Elections Act 1991` decision
            , `sch 6 para 1(i) the appeal is made under one of the eight provisions named` provision
            , `sch 6 para 1(j) the appeal is made under a written law that provides for the appeal to lie to the Court of Appeal` `the appeal is made under a written law that provides for the appeal to lie to the Court of Appeal`
            , `sch 6 para 1(k) the appeal is against a decision or order under the Mediation Act 2017` decision
            , `sch 6 para 1(l) the appeal is against a decision or order under the Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020` decision)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): para 1 speaks of "a decision of the General Division in the exercise of its original or appellate civil jurisdiction"
    ELSE NOTHING
